{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790110236,"nonce":"PkWT45Y+2Gg8d/jur9cra2jCT2w=","title":"Decided 2026-09-22 with Luis.","message":"1. Ref namespaces carry a `work-` prefix so they read as git-work's next to other refs: refs/work-issues, refs/work-iterations, refs/work-schema (fields, types and relations, one entity each, kind in the create op), refs/work-views, refs/work-flows. Flat with a prefix rather than refs/work/\u003ckind\u003e/, because identities are pinned flat by the pristine package and a slash in a namespace also names clock and cache files. The provisional refs/issues-v5 is dropped: the peer entity goes straight to refs/work-issues, so the migration (bf6f392) has no rename step; it reads refs/issues/* as bugs, writes refs/work-issues/*, deletes the old refs locally and on origin.\n\n2. Identities move to refs/work-identities in the same flag day. This IS an edit to a pristine package: three string constants in entities/identity/identity.go (identityRefPattern, identityRemoteRefPattern, Namespace); the identity clocks are not namespace-named. Judged the smallest possible exception and worth it for a uniform prefix; AGENTS.md lists it as the one exception to the pristine seven. Not edited yet: the live refs must be renamed with it.\n\n3. Query language is jq via github.com/itchyny/gojq (replaces git-bug's query package; reshapes 3c9c24d). The program runs over the same JSON `--format json` prints, so the excerpt shape is the query contract. Measured on synthetic excerpts, compiled once: filter+sort 1.2 ms / 1k issues, 14 ms / 10k; group_by report 1.7 ms / 17 ms. Weakness accepted: a mistyped field name is null, not an error; soften by checking referenced field names against the schema before running.\n\n4. Immutable non-hash ids (e.g. Jira keys) are aliases, not entity ids: the entity id stays the hash of the create op (pristine entity.Id is 64 hex). An alias is create-op metadata, content-addressed at import or first-write-wins via SetMetadata after export, indexed by the excerpt, accepted wherever an id is, shown beside the hash, uniqueness enforced on write in the cache. Jira is the sequential-id coordinator we already have; no second local alias scheme.\n\n5. Views and flows stay separate kinds sharing one concept, a named selection (a jq program plus sort): a view is selection + presentation (read-only, live-evaluable); a flow is selection + actions + optional trigger (close sprint, move unfinished issues, ...). A flow with a trigger is what 221b629 called a rule, so rules fold into flows and there is no refs/work-rules.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790110236,"nonce":"NGgrgEMbgvZ5VolOrv1Igukmr6g=","key":"type","value":"decision"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790110236,"nonce":"tLLxu53DUvIKuivpy74hKj9abNw=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}